      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good catch.\n\nIn practice right now it\u0027s a no-op, because while we store the request in the IpServer, nothing uses it. While we might use the request in a future CL, I think we can cross that bridge when we come to it, and keep this CL as is.\n\nAlternatives:\n1. Check here if the request is a legacy request, and if so pass in null instead.\n2. When legacyTether is called, pass down a null request.\n\nAs you point out, because passing the request down as this CL currently does is an improvement over passing null. Since this is actually a no-op, I\u0027d prefer to keep the code as is. Thoughts?",
